# Coordinate-matched calibration v2 amendment

Added after v1 execution but before accepting or recording a research cycle.
The v1 rows used independent RFF seeds for the coordinate-matched and
double-width arms.  That is valid for marginal method comparisons but confounds
the frozen prediction about the effect of changing RFF allocation.  The v1
files and successful receipt remain retained as preliminary/unaccepted
evidence.

V2 changes only this point: within each data/draw/`ell`, both RFF arms use the
same frequency seed, so the `R=ell/2` frequencies are the prefix of the
`R=ell` draw.  Data, tuning, permutation and Nyström seeds, widths, sample
sizes, exact reference, costs, thresholds and all interpretation boundaries
remain unchanged.  V2 writes distinct result files and additionally reports
the median within-pair error ratio and the fraction of pairs meeting the 1.25
materiality threshold.  This repair was selected from code/protocol inspection,
not from a preferred numerical direction.

